WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.139
Reinforcement learning promises optimal decisions,

00:00:03.219 --> 00:00:07.451
but almost every algorithm quietly assumes the
world never changes.

00:00:07.531 --> 00:00:11.764
In real settings like mobile health, traffic
control, and robotics,

00:00:11.844 --> 00:00:17.558
that stationarity assumption breaks down over time
and quietly poisons the learned policy.

00:00:17.638 --> 00:00:23.029
This paper introduces a doubly robust statistical
test that checks whether an offline

00:00:23.109 --> 00:00:26.055
Markov decision process is actually stationary,

00:00:26.135 --> 00:00:28.050
and pinpoints where it changes.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:33.264
The test pairs modern machine learning estimators
with semiparametric statistics,

00:00:33.344 --> 00:00:39.508
so it controls false alarms while staying powerful
even when the state space is high dimensional.

00:00:39.588 --> 00:00:43.049
Across four simulations and a real intern health study,

00:00:43.129 --> 00:00:50.580
it detects change points others miss and lets
policies recover the reward that non stationarity would otherwise cost.
